<title>FRANCE: Bull 1996 net up 23 percent.</title>
<headline>Bull 1996 net up 23 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				376   vs	306</p>
<p>    Operating profit			780   vs	849</p>
<p>Net financial charges and other</p>
<p>	profits and losses		  404   vs	543</p>
<p>    Turnover			     24,049   vs   26,656</p>
<p>    Net debt				1,985   vs    2,144</p>
<p>NOTE - Bull gave the results in a statement. It said it had a net loss of 612 million francs in the first half of 1996, including 661 million francs in non-recurring losses related to personal computers and electronic cards.</p>
</text>
